.TH MORE 1 Nexix
.SH NAME
more \- read text a screen at a time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B more
[ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Display a text file or standard input on the terminal.
Use space, f or control-F for the next page; b or control-B for the previous
page; j, return or down-arrow for the next line; k or up-arrow for the
previous line; d/control-D and u/control-U for half-page movement.
Use g/home to return to the beginning and G/end to reach the last page.
Page-up and page-down keys are also accepted.
.PP
Type / followed by text and return to search forward, or ? to search backward.
Searches are literal and case-sensitive. An empty search repeats the previous
pattern. Use n to repeat in the same direction and N for the opposite direction.
Escape cancels search entry. Type q to quit, or h for a reminder of the keys.
.PP
When standard output is redirected, copy the input without screen controls.
Interactive display removes nroff overstrikes, expands tabs, wraps long lines
and renders document control bytes harmlessly. Terminal state is restored on
quit, input/output errors and catchable termination signals.
Input and decoded text are limited to 4 MiB; allocation failures are reported.
.PP
The terminal must provide cursor motion and clearing through termcap.
Unsupported terminals receive plain output.
.SH SEE ALSO
man(1), clear(1)
